(version 1)

# JLCPCB splits hole rules by feature; KiCad has one global each, set to the via case.
# A silently-dropped rule looks identical to a passing board, so verify by A/B, not by exit code.

# Hole to track is published per plating class, PTH 0.28 mm and NPTH 0.20 mm, so the
# condition below is deliberately plated-only. NPTH is already held by the 0.20 mm built-in
# hole clearance in board setup, which is the JLCPCB NPTH figure exactly. Widening this to
# !A.isPlated() applies the plated number to J1's mechanical pegs and raises a false error on
# the VBUS pair at 0.2052 mm, which meets the NPTH spec. Verified by probe, both !A.isPlated()
# and A.Pad_Type == 'NPTH, mechanical' match those pegs; neither belongs on this rule.
(rule "PTH hole to copper"
	(constraint hole_clearance (min 0.28mm))
	(severity error)
	(condition "A.Pad_Type == 'Through-hole'"))

(rule "PTH hole to PTH hole"
	(constraint hole_to_hole (min 0.45mm))
	(severity error)
	(condition "A.Pad_Type == 'Through-hole' && B.Pad_Type == 'Through-hole'"))

# The nRESET west channel rule was deleted 2026-08-04. It named the rule area
# 'U1 west escape channel', which did not survive the 12.600 mm re-layout, so the rule matched
# nothing and reported nothing while looking identical to a rule that held. The channel it
# described is the antenna coupling gap now and nRESET does not cross it: AC13 leaves through
# an in-pad via, not planar. Do not re-add it without re-adding the area and A/B-ing by name.

# Design rule 29: the RF line is a grounded coplanar waveguide with the pour held 0.220 mm
# back from each edge. Nothing else on the board holds that once a zone is filled, and a pour
# flooded at the RF50 net class 0.150 mm puts the line at 42 ohm. Scoped to zones so the
# 0.172 mm signal-to-ground gap inside the 0201 shunt lands does not raise a false error.
# Outer layers only, added 2026-08-04. The setback is the coplanar side gap and belongs on the
# face the line is drawn on. Unscoped it also cut a 0.840 mm void out of In1.Cu and In2.Cu at
# the face-change via, removing 0.855 mm of the line's own reference. A/B the fill after any
# edit here: if the layer token is rejected the rule drops and the pour floods to 0.150 mm,
# which reads as a passing board. The check is the nearest GND fill vertex to RF copper,
# 0.2205 mm on F.Cu and on B.Cu.
#
# Rule 29's line width is amended here on 2026-08-04 and the setback is not. The rule reads
# 0.360 mm of line on both faces and the board cannot build that on B.Cu. The antenna band
# tiles 'antenna band, B.Cu 4' and 'antenna band, B.Cu 5' forbid tracks and leave a 0.320 mm
# feed window at record x 1.100 to 1.300 by y 8.040 to 8.360, so a 0.360 mm line enters both
# tiles by 0.020 mm and raises items_not_allowed. What is drawn is 0.150 mm over the whole
# 1.000 mm B.Cu run from the face change into the radiator, 41.7 percent of the specified
# width, and it is rule 31's landing neck rather than a transcription error. The amended
# reading: 0.360 mm governs F.Cu and any B.Cu run east of the antenna band; the last 1.000 mm
# on B.Cu is 0.150 mm and is not a 50 ohm section.
#
# The impedance consequence, computed on this stackup's 0.2104 mm of 7628 at er 4.4 with the
# Hammerstad-Jensen thickness correction. A 0.150 mm line reads 74.80 ohm against 50.49 ohm at
# 0.360 mm, and over 1.000 mm, 5.20 degrees at 2.44 GHz, that section between 50 ohm
# terminations is VSWR 1.078 and 28.5 dB of return loss against VSWR 1.002 at full width. The
# 0.076 of VSWR it costs sits inside JLCPCB's own plus or minus 10 percent control band, which
# design.md prices at VSWR 1.09 on its own. Read 74.80 ohm as a floor rather than a figure:
# In1.Cu and In2.Cu both stop at x 1.300 and the face-change via's own antipad covers the rest,
# so all 1.000 mm of that run has no reference plane and is not a controlled-impedance line at
# all, which is the second reason widening it buys less than the arithmetic suggests.
# Measured on the delivered board, 1.3003 mm of the 2.1870 mm drawn feed, 59.5 percent, has no
# inner reference. Widening the notch is the alternative and it is NOT taken: it moves the
# ground edge next to the radiator feed point, which is an antenna change, and design.md's own
# next-step 8 forbids it while the match is solved for the neck.
(rule "RF corridor coplanar setback"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.22mm))
	(layer outer)
	(severity error)
	(condition "(A.NetName == 'RF_50' || A.NetName == 'ANT_FEED' || A.NetName == 'RF_CHIP') && B.Type == 'Zone'"))

# XC2 leaves U1.A23 and DEC4_6 leaves U1.E24 into the B.Cu pocket between U1's north outer
# ring at y 7.473 and the decoupling row C5 and C4 at y 7.838, which is 0.365 mm of strip.
# Both nets are Default class and every wall of that pocket is GND, which is Power class, so
# the pair resolves to 0.150 mm and the widest path either net reaches is 0.070 mm, under the
# 0.090 mm track floor. At 0.090 mm the same path opens. The figure is JLCPCB's own spacing
# floor and sits above IPC-2221 B2's 0.10 mm for 0 to 15 V only in the sense that both these
# nets are sub-2 V internal regulator and crystal nodes carrying no rail potential. Scoped by
# net pair and by the B.Cu rule area. The area itself was lost in the re-layout and was redrawn
# on 2026-08-04, B.Cu, record x 6.150 to 8.450 by y 6.550 to 8.350, all five keepout flags off.
# Prove it loaded by A/B rather than by exit code: a 0.090 mm XC2 stub at 0.100 mm from C5's
# GND land inside the area passes with this file and raises one clearance error without it.
(rule "U1 north pocket crystal and decoupling escape"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.09mm))
	(severity error)
	(condition "(A.NetName == 'XC2' || A.NetName == 'DEC4_6') && B.NetName == 'GND' && A.insideArea('U1 north pocket')"))


# NextPCB Advanced HDI: 3 mil minimum trace/space for the B.Cu-to-In4 microvia escape.
# Until 2026-08-10 this rule and "3+2+3 sequential microvia geometry" both read
# "A.Via_Type == 'Micro' || B.Via_Type == 'Micro' || A.Layer == 'In5.Cu' || ... In6.Cu ...".
# A bare layer test matches every object on that layer, so track to track, track to zone and
# zone to zone on In5.Cu and In6.Cu all resolved to 0.08 mm against netclasses of 0.09 mm
# Default and 0.15 mm Power, USB, RF50 and VBUS, and the OR on Via_Type relaxed every pad,
# track and zone that merely stood next to a microvia. Two whole layers and every microvia
# neighbourhood ran at 3 mil while the comment claimed an escape-proof scope.
# The two rules were byte-identical in their constraints and the second condition contained the
# first, so they are one rule now, narrowed to the microvia pair the comment always described.
# Narrowing exposes 351 clearance and 263 hole_clearance reports that were previously hidden,
# including the board's true hole-to-copper minimum of 0.0805 mm at J1's west NPTH peg. Those
# are board defects, not rule defects. Do NOT re-widen this to make the report quiet.
# A/B it by name after any edit: deleting this rule takes the clearance count from 485 to 499,
# so 14 reports is the entire job it does and anything larger means the scope slipped again.
(rule "NextPCB HDI microvia clearance"
    (constraint clearance (min 0.08mm))
    (constraint hole_clearance (min 0.08mm))
    (severity error)
    (condition "A.Via_Type == 'Micro' && B.Via_Type == 'Micro'"))


# HDI RF superseding rule: the B.Cu RF_50 section is a masked microstrip over
# the adjacent In4 GND plane.  The rule-area polygon is drawn for 0.310 mm;
# 0.300 mm here is the hard copper-edge release floor after fill tessellation.
(rule "NextPCB HDI RF_50 B.Cu width"
    (constraint track_width (min 0.115mm) (max 0.115mm))
    (severity error)
    (condition "A.NetName == 'RF_50' && A.Layer == 'B.Cu'"))
(rule "NextPCB HDI RF_50 same-side GND setback"
    (constraint clearance (min 0.300mm))
    (severity error)
    (condition "A.NetName == 'RF_50' && A.Layer == 'B.Cu' && B.Type == 'Zone' && A.insideArea('RF corridor, RF_50')"))


# Drill separation between vias, laser drills included. The rule this replaces,
# "HDI all-via physical drill separation", used physical_hole_clearance and measured no such
# thing. KiCad defines physical_hole_clearance as one hole's diameter to another object's BODY,
# so a via pair reads centre distance minus one hole radius minus the partner's pad radius. The
# marker that read actual 0.0140 mm sits on centres 0.1890 mm apart, 0.1890 - 0.050 - 0.125,
# and the drill separation there is 0.0890 mm. hole_to_hole is the true hole-to-hole measure and
# it skips laser drills by design; probed at min 0.9 mm over every via pair it returned 48
# markers, every one of them pairing a mechanical drill with something, none microvia to
# microvia. That rule also reported nothing at all once the microvia relaxation above was
# narrowed, because DRC stops emitting a given violation type at about 200 markers per run and
# the built-in hole clearance check consumed the whole budget before it ran.
#
# physical_clearance measures pad edge to pad edge, and drill separation is the reported actual
# plus the two annular rings. 223 vias carry 0.075 mm of ring at 0.250 over 0.100 and 0.300 over
# 0.150, and 18 carry 0.090 mm at 0.330 over 0.150, so the offset is 0.150 mm for a pair of
# 0.075 rings and 0.165 or 0.180 mm where a 0.330 mm via is involved. NextPCB's different-net
# row is 12 mil, 0.300 mm, against conductive anodic filament, and their same-net row is 8 mil,
# 0.200 mm. The minima below take the 0.150 mm offset, which is exact for a 0.075 pair and
# strict by 0.015 to 0.030 mm for a 0.330 mm via, so the rule over-reports and never misses:
# one pair sits at 0.3000 mm of true separation and is reported. Read every actual as a floor of
# 0.150 mm below the drill figure and re-derive the offsets if any via padstack changes.
#
# Physical clearance is tested only between objects that share a layer, so two vias in different
# dielectrics are not compared and do not need to be, their drills never meet. The same-net rule
# reports the intentional sequential stacks at actual 0.0000; they are the manifest's allowed
# markers and they now carry type clearance rather than hole_clearance.
(rule "via drill separation, different nets"
    (constraint physical_clearance (min 0.150mm))
    (severity error)
    (condition "A.Type == 'Via' && B.Type == 'Via' && A.Net != B.Net"))

(rule "via drill separation, same net"
    (constraint physical_clearance (min 0.050mm))
    (severity error)
    (condition "A.Type == 'Via' && B.Type == 'Via' && A.Net == B.Net"))
